I confirmed the answer directly in the source: `order_service.mark_paid` updates the order's status to `"paid"` via `order_repo.update_status`, writes an outbox event, but never calls `cache.invalidate_order` (or `cache.invalidate`) — unlike the sibling `cancel_order` function, which explicitly calls `cache.invalidate_order(order_id)` after its status change. The code even contains an explicit comment flagging this as a planted bug.

This means any previously cached `order:{order_id}` entry (populated by `get_order`) will keep returning the stale pre-payment status after `mark_paid` runs, directly violating README invariant I4 ("Order cache entries are invalidated on any status change").

